# Every entry here is a deliberate, documented exception — not a blanket
# suppression. Each one names why it can't be fixed by a normal dependency
# bump in this repo, and what would make it revisit-able.

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964: msgpack HIGH severity, installed 1.1.2, fixed 1.2.1.
# This is pip's own vendored copy (pip/_vendor/msgpack) shipped inside the
# pip package itself, not an independently pip-installable top-level
# dependency of this app — `pip install --upgrade msgpack` doesn't touch
# it. Confirmed as of pip 26.2.1 (the newest release on PyPI at the time
# this was added) that upstream still vendors the unpatched copy; pip's
# own `main` branch has already bumped the vendored version to 1.2.1, so
# this should resolve itself on pip's next release. Revisit by removing
# this line and confirming Trivy comes back clean.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# CVE-2025-47273 / CVE-2026-59890: setuptools HIGH+MEDIUM, both reported
# against "Installed Version: 70.3.0" — a version that is not actually in
# this image. The Dockerfile explicitly upgrades to setuptools>=83.0.0 and
# deletes any stale dist-info left behind by the base image; this was
# verified three separate ways before concluding it's a Trivy-side bug
# rather than a real finding:
#   1. A debug build step ran an unrestricted filesystem search
#      (no path/mount restrictions) for anything setuptools-related —
#      the only matches were setuptools-83.0.0.dist-info and the package
#      itself. No 70.3.0 anywhere.
#   2. `pip list` inside the built image reports only `setuptools 83.0.0`.
#   3. Trivy's own `--list-all-pkgs` package inventory correctly lists
#      setuptools-83.0.0.dist-info/METADATA — but its separate
#      vulnerability-matching table still cross-references the same
#      package against 70.3.0. That's an internal inconsistency between
#      Trivy's detection and matching logic, not a real installed
#      version, and it reproduces identically on both the action's
#      default Trivy binary (v0.70.0) and the latest release (v0.73.0)
#      at the time this was added.
# Revisit periodically by removing these two lines and confirming Trivy
# still reports them cleanly resolved (or file/check for an upstream
# aquasecurity/trivy issue if it still doesn't).
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-59890
